# Copy to .env.local and fill in. Until these are set the app runs on the stub
# repository: real structure, no data, and the sign-in page says "Not configured".
#
# On Vercel these two live in the project's Environment Variables, not in a file — see
# "Deploying" in ../README.md. The VITE_ prefix is load-bearing and it is the FRAMEWORK's,
# not Supabase's: Vite exposes only VITE_-prefixed variables to client code. A Supabase
# integration told the framework is Next.js provisions NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL and
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY instead — names `import.meta.env` cannot see at all, so
# the build goes green, the site serves, and sign-in reports "Not configured" while the
# dashboard shows the values sitting right there. Tell the integration it is Vite.
#
# These two names are the only ones read. app/src/data/supabaseEnv.ts once carried a
# fallback to a second spelling; it was removed on 6 September after the live bundle
# proved neither fallback name was set.
#
# The key is the publishable one (`sb_publishable_…`) from Supabase's API settings.
# Never put the service role key here or anywhere else with a VITE_ prefix — it
# bypasses RLS, and a VITE_ variable is public the moment it is built.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
